[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: ReqAML — Requirements
UID: reqaml-requirements
COMMENT: >>>
client: Raby-Family (raby-family)
project: ReqAML (reqaml)
ReqAML dogfood export — StrictDoc interchange only
schema_version: 2026-10-06
<<<

[SECTION]
UID: SEC-IA
TITLE: Identity & Access
STATEMENT: >>>
Identity and access actions for ReqAML — SSO sign-in/out, client scoped view, profile, and project grant administration.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
KIND: section
LEVEL: 1
VERSION_UID: SEC-IA
STATUS: active
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: A01
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Sign in via SSO
STATEMENT: >>>
A user signs in via enterprise SSO (OIDC or SAML). ReqAML validates the IdP token, establishes a least-privilege session, loads grants, and emits an auditable sign-in event.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
KIND: requirement
BASE_UID: A01
VERSION_N: 0
rbac_op: auth:signin
priority: 10
iteration: iter-r0
security.catalog_ref: NIST-IA
security.verification_note: NIST IA/AC/AU families apply (IA-2, AC-3, AU-2/3/12). STIG TBD ASD V6R4. No local password store; MFA at IdP.
edge: ← satisfies from CAP-SSO
edge: ← conforms_to from CTL-AC-3
edge: ← refines from ARCH-OTEL
edge: ← refines from MC01
in_scope_of_contract: Design-2026-10
delivered_by_release: R0-sequences
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: A02
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Sign out
STATEMENT: >>>
An authenticated user signs out. ReqAML terminates the server session, clears the client session handle, and records an auditable logout event.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
KIND: requirement
BASE_UID: A02
VERSION_N: 0
rbac_op: auth:signout
priority: 20
iteration: iter-r0
security.catalog_ref: NIST-AC
security.verification_note: NIST AC-12 session termination; AU-2/3/12 logout audit. STIG TBD ASD V6R4.
edge: ← satisfies from CAP-SSO
in_scope_of_contract: Design-2026-10
delivered_by_release: R0-sequences
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: A03
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Select Client Scoped View
STATEMENT: >>>
An authenticated user selects a Client Scoped View. The active clientId is persisted server-side so subsequent queries are bound to that client for least privilege.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
KIND: requirement
BASE_UID: A03
VERSION_N: 0
rbac_op: client:scope:select
priority: 10
iteration: iter-r0
security.catalog_ref: NIST-AC
security.verification_note: NIST AC-3/AC-6 least privilege via server-bound scope. STIG TBD ASD V6R4.
edge: refines → ARCH-CP-HIER
edge: ← satisfies from CAP-SCOPED-VIEW
edge: ← conforms_to from CTL-AC-3
in_scope_of_contract: Design-2026-10
delivered_by_release: R0-sequences
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: A04
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Clear / change Scoped View
STATEMENT: >>>
A user clears or changes Client Scoped View. ReqAML updates or clears the server-side active client binding and audits the scope change.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
KIND: requirement
BASE_UID: A04
VERSION_N: 0
rbac_op: client:scope:clear
priority: 30
iteration: iter-r0
security.catalog_ref: NIST-AC
security.verification_note: NIST AC-3 access enforcement on scope clear/change. STIG TBD ASD V6R4.
edge: ← satisfies from CAP-SCOPED-VIEW
in_scope_of_contract: Design-2026-10
delivered_by_release: R0-sequences
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: A05
STATUS: Active
TITLE: View own profile / grants
STATEMENT: >>>
A user views their own profile and project grants. ReqAML returns only the caller’s identity and grants (no cross-subject disclosure).
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
KIND: requirement
BASE_UID: A05
VERSION_N: 0
rbac_op: identity:read_self
priority: 40
iteration: iter-r0
security.catalog_ref: NIST-AC
security.verification_note: NIST AC-3 self-read boundary; AU for access logging where required. STIG TBD ASD V6R4.
edge: ← satisfies from CAP-RBAC
in_scope_of_contract: Design-2026-10
delivered_by_release: R0-sequences
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: A06
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Invite / link identity
STATEMENT: >>>
An admin invites or links an identity to a client or project. ReqAML records the external subject binding and audits who linked whom.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
KIND: requirement
BASE_UID: A06
VERSION_N: 0
rbac_op: identity:link
priority: 50
iteration: iter-r0
security.catalog_ref: NIST-IA
security.verification_note: NIST IA-2/AC-2 account/identity linkage; AU-2/3/12 admin actions. STIG TBD ASD V6R4.
edge: ← satisfies from CAP-RBAC
in_scope_of_contract: Design-2026-10
delivered_by_release: R0-sequences
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: A07
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Grant project role
STATEMENT: >>>
A project admin grants a role on a project to an identity. ReqAML creates a project_grant row and audits the grant (actor, subject, role).
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
KIND: requirement
BASE_UID: A07
VERSION_N: 0
rbac_op: project:grant:create
priority: 50
iteration: iter-r0
security.catalog_ref: NIST-AC
security.verification_note: NIST AC-2/AC-3/AC-6 grant administration. STIG TBD ASD V6R4.
edge: ← satisfies from CAP-RBAC
in_scope_of_contract: Design-2026-10
delivered_by_release: R0-sequences
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: A08
STATUS: Active
