[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
UID: SEC-CP
TITLE: Client & Project
STATEMENT: >>>
Client owns projects; all project work assumes a Client Scoped View.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
KIND: section
LEVEL: 1
VERSION_UID: SEC-CP
STATUS: active
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ARCH-CP-HIER
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Client → Project hierarchy
STATEMENT: >>>
ReqAML organizes work as Client → Project. Projects belong to exactly one client; Client Scoped View is assumed for most project operations.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
KIND: requirement
BASE_UID: ARCH-CP-HIER
VERSION_N: 0
priority: 5
edge: ← uses from ARCH-UI
edge: ← refines from A03
in_scope_of_contract: Design-2026-10
<<<

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
UID: SEC-RL
TITLE: Requirement Lines & Versions
STATEMENT: >>>
Requirement lines are stable tree nodes; requirement versions hold statement and status.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
KIND: section
LEVEL: 1
VERSION_UID: SEC-RL
STATUS: active
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ARCH-VER
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Static .N requirement versioning
STATEMENT: >>>
Each requirement line has versions with UIDs base_uid or base_uid.N (static append). Children stay on the parent line (parent = base_uid); there is no cascade fork. Obsolete/withdrawn is a new version with that status.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
KIND: requirement
BASE_UID: ARCH-VER
VERSION_N: 0
priority: 5
edge: ← uses from ARCH-API
in_scope_of_contract: Design-2026-10
<<<

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
UID: SEC-CT
TITLE: Contracts
STATEMENT: >>>
Contracts are junction overlays that mark requirement versions in_scope_of a named agreement.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
KIND: section
LEVEL: 1
VERSION_UID: SEC-CT
STATUS: active
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ARCH-CONTRACT
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Contracts as overlays
STATEMENT: >>>
Contracts are related overlays, not tree parents. A contract links requirement version UIDs via in_scope_of; document views filter by contract and optionally walk parent lines for context.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
KIND: requirement
BASE_UID: ARCH-CONTRACT
VERSION_N: 0
priority: 15
in_scope_of_contract: Design-2026-10
<<<

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
UID: SEC-REL
TITLE: Releases
STATEMENT: >>>
Releases snapshot the requirement versions they deliver; they are not tree parents.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
KIND: section
LEVEL: 1
VERSION_UID: SEC-REL
STATUS: active
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ARCH-RELEASE
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Releases deliver version snapshots
STATEMENT: >>>
A release delivers a snapshot of requirement version UIDs. Shipping freezes the delivered set; releases do not own the requirement tree.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
KIND: requirement
BASE_UID: ARCH-RELEASE
VERSION_N: 0
priority: 15
in_scope_of_contract: Design-2026-10
